│ patch_description        │ Replace the clipped concentric-ring layout with a staggered near-hexagonal seed and a     │
│                          │ deterministic constrained local optimization over all centers and radii. The staggered    │
│                          │ rows provide substantially better initial density than the previous outer ring, whose     │
│                          │ clipped centers created many nearly coincident circles.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The optimization directly maximizes the total radius subject to all four wall constraints │
│                          │ per circle and every pairwise non-overlap constraint. Several small deterministic         │
│                          │ perturbations of the geometric seed are used because boundary effects and unequal radii   │
│                          │ can lead to different local optima. Analytic constraint derivatives keep SLSQP practical. │
│                          │ Finally, a global feasibility rescaling is applied from the actual returned geometry;     │
│                          │ this preserves the optimized relative radii while protecting against floating-point       │
│                          │ constraint tolerances.                                                                    │
