│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ nonlinear_packing_refinement                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the clipped concentric-ring arrangement with a feasible layered near-hexagonal    │
│                          │ seed and a deterministic constrained nonlinear refinement. The seed uses alternating rows │
│                          │ of five and six circles, with larger circles in the less crowded rows and smaller circles │
│                          │ in the six-circle rows. This already avoids the severe boundary clipping and coincident   │
│                          │ outer-circle failures of the old constructor.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The refinement directly maximizes the sum of the 26 independent radii subject to all four │
│                          │ wall constraints per circle and all pairwise non-overlap constraints. Supplying analytic  │
│                          │ constraint Jacobians makes SLSQP practical for this relatively small 78-variable problem. │
│                          │ A final uniform safety scaling is applied from the exact geometric clearances, ensuring   │
│                          │ that tiny optimizer feasibility tolerances can never create an invalid output. If SciPy   │
│                          │ is unavailable or optimization fails, the valid layered seed is returned.                 │
