│ patch_name               │ diverse_multistart_seeds                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Expand the deterministic multistart strategy rather than relying on four closely related  │
│                          │ sinusoidal perturbations of one five-row topology.  The sum-of-radii problem has many     │
│                          │ locally optimal contact graphs: the existing 5/6/5/6/4 layered seed is useful, but a      │
│                          │ six-row truncated triangular lattice can converge to a distinct boundary-contact pattern. │
│                          │ Retaining all original starts guarantees no regression from the prior search, while       │
│                          │ adding reproducible independent perturbations around both seeds gives SLSQP substantially │
│                          │ more opportunities to discover an asymmetric packing near or above the 2.635 reference.   │
│                          │ The number of variables and constraints remains small, and the added starts are well      │
│                          │ within the evaluator timeout.                                                             │
