│ patch_description        │ Replace the single five-row seed with several related staggered row profiles.             │
│                          │ Unequal-radius optima are sensitive to the boundary contact graph: moving the six-circle  │
│                          │ row between vertical layers, or using a six-row truncated triangular lattice, changes     │
│                          │ which circles can profitably touch walls and which interior contacts become active.  The  │
│                          │ existing deterministic phase perturbations are retained for each profile.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Initialize each optimization with radii derived from each center's local geometric        │
│                          │ clearance rather than a uniform radius.  This gives SLSQP useful scale variation between  │
│                          │ boundary and interior circles while maintaining a strictly feasible initial               │
│                          │ configuration.  The number of starts remains modest (20), well within the timeout given   │
│                          │ the current sub-second four-start runtime.                                                │
