│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multistart_nonlinear_packing                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the clipped concentric-ring construction with a deterministic multistart          │
│                          │ nonlinear optimization seeded by staggered hexagonal rows. The optimization treats        │
│                          │ centers and radii jointly, enforcing every wall and pairwise non-overlap constraint       │
│                          │ directly. This permits boundary circles and interior circles to acquire different radii,  │
│                          │ which is essential for improving beyond a uniform-radius lattice.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each SLSQP run starts from a slightly perturbed layered hexagonal arrangement. Radii are  │
│                          │ initialized from the fixed-center linear program rather than from uniformly tiny values,  │
│                          │ giving the nonlinear solver useful information about local wall and neighbor clearance.   │
│                          │ The best valid optimized center configuration is then passed through the linear radius    │
│                          │ maximization routine and slightly shrunk for robust evaluator validity.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
