│ patch_name               │ lp_radius_recovery                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the global-radius scaling certification with a fixed-center linear program.  For  │
│                          │ any candidate center configuration, the radii subproblem is linear: each radius is capped │
│                          │ by its nearest wall, and every pair imposes `r_i + r_j <= distance(i,j)`.  The existing   │
│                          │ common scaling discards uneven-radius improvements whenever one nearly active constraint  │
│                          │ has optimizer roundoff.  Solving this small 26-variable LP recovers the best feasible     │
│                          │ unequal radii for the optimized centers, especially improving boundary-layer              │
│                          │ configurations.  A small margin makes the returned packing strictly valid.                │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0361                                                                                   │
