                        Patch Metadata - Gen 26/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lp_radius_reoptimization                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ For a fixed set of centers, the optimal radii are obtained from a linear program: each    │
│                          │ radius has a wall upper bound, and every pair contributes the linear inequality r_i + r_j │
│                          │ <= distance(i,j). The nonlinear SLSQP stage can stop with a suboptimal radius allocation  │
│                          │ even when its centers are promising, especially in asymmetric defect layouts. Re-solving  │
│                          │ this small LP after every center optimization extracts the best feasible varying-radius   │
│                          │ allocation from that contact geometry. The existing common-scale polish is retained       │
│                          │ afterward to certify strict feasibility against numerical tolerances.                     │
