│ patch_name               │ layered_seed_portfolio                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single 5,6,5,6,4 lattice initialization with a portfolio centered on the      │
│                          │ stronger five-row 5,6,5,5,5 contact graph and its vertical reversals and boundary-defect  │
│                          │ variants.  The prior initialization has overly tight five-circle rows for radius 0.1,     │
│                          │ whereas these seeds are deliberately feasible at small radius and allow SLSQP to choose   │
│                          │ unequal boundary radii.  Independent row phases and asymmetric left/right margins expose  │
│                          │ contact graphs that reflection-symmetric starts tend to miss.  The optimizer still        │
│                          │ retains restarts around its incumbent arrangement, but now first explores materially      │
│                          │ different layered geometries.                                                             │
