│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ layered_seed_portfolio                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace several nearly identical random restarts of the initial `(5,6,5,6,4)` lattice     │
│                          │ with a controlled portfolio of asymmetric five-row contact graphs.  The principal         │
│                          │ improvement opportunity is at the boundary: moving the six-circle row or a four-circle    │
│                          │ defect changes which circles can expand against square sides and corners.  Independently  │
│                          │ varying the left and right row margins additionally breaks reflection symmetry without    │
│                          │ relying solely on random noise.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The portfolio retains the proven hexagonal layering geometry, uses conservative initial   │
│                          │ radii, and reserves later attempts for perturbations around the best discovered contact   │
│                          │ graph.  This increases the chance that SLSQP enters a basin associated with the           │
│                          │ approximately `2.635` asymmetric construction while preserving the existing execution     │
│                          │ budget and public interface.                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
