│ patch_description        │ Add exact constraint derivatives and replace the final SLSQP radius allocation by the     │
│                          │ fixed-center linear-program optimum. The geometric optimization determines a contact      │
│                          │ graph, but its terminating radius vector is often not the best allocation on that graph:  │
│                          │ the LP can deliberately shrink a poorly placed boundary disk and distribute the released  │
│                          │ clearance to several neighbors. Analytic derivatives make the existing multistart         │
│                          │ optimization more reliable and leave ample time for a short second polish from that       │
│                          │ LP-optimal allocation. The strict existing common-scale polish remains the final validity │
