│ patch_description        │ The previous constructor used 24 broadly similar SLSQP runs with 700 iterations and       │
│                          │ retained only the single best LP-certified result. This version uses a two-stage          │
│                          │ strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Exploration stage:** 20 deterministic layered and triangular-lattice seeds, with     │
│                          │ asymmetric perturbations, are optimized for 600 iterations.                               │
│                          │ 2. **LP certification and structural selection:** each candidate is reallocated using an  │
│                          │ exact fixed-center linear program. Candidates are ranked by LP sum, raw nonlinear         │
│                          │ objective, contact-count diagnostics, and distinct near-active contact signatures.        │
│                          │ 3. **Polishing stage:** the best structurally different candidates are restarted from     │
│                          │ their LP-optimal radii and given 2400 additional SLSQP iterations. This focuses expensive │
│                          │ optimization on promising contact graphs instead of spending all iterations on            │
│                          │ near-duplicate row arrangements.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main changed parameters are: more diverse row templates, 20 initial starts instead of │
│                          │ 24 nearly related starts, 600 initial iterations, up to 8 structurally distinct           │
│                          │ refinement candidates, 2400 polishing iterations, tighter LP-start scaling, and a smaller │
│                          │ final safety margin.                                                                      │
